My experience suggests the limit is 3/2x the monster's "minimum" level
(a full-grown dragon is at least a lvl 15 monster, and a dragon can
advance to lvl 22). Such limits may be exceeded if a monster can "grow
up" - little dog can advance to dog, soldier to sergeant, baby dragon
to adult dragon etc.
Monsters can also advance to "excessive" levels by eating wraith
corpses (this has a limit of minimum level +15) and by quaffing
potions of gain level (limit of lvl 49 reachable this way, regardless
of minimum level; but not every monster will use potions, or eat
corpses).

